kijai/ComfyUI-SolAttn_triton
  https://github.com/kijai/ComfyUI-SolAttn_triton

  A Triton implementation of Sol-Attn for ComfyUI.  No code from it is used
  here -- that repository publishes no license, and this project's backend is
  torch flex_attention rather than Triton -- but reading it is what prompted
  four things in this implementation, and the credit for noticing them is
  theirs:

    * Morton (Z-order) reordering of the video span, so an attention block is
      a compact 3D neighbourhood rather than a thin strip of one frame, and
      the observation that a model with non-uniform frame spacing wants a
      per-frame 2D curve rather than a 3D one.
    * Applying Sol-Attn's approximate correction on top of a block-sparse
      executor by merging it with the exact partial softmax.
    * A Cornish-Fisher expansion of the routing quantile in place of the
      plain Gaussian one.
    * Publishing the true transformer block index from module hooks, and the
      observation that the last block is as approximation-sensitive as the
      first.

  The implementations of all four here were written against this project's
  own flex_attention backend and ComfyUI's MiniMax H3 source.
